{# "We have it." Sent to whoever used the contact form.

   Not optional. Somebody who writes to a project and hears nothing assumes it
   went nowhere, and the second thing they do is give up. This also carries the
   reference number, which is the only way they can chase it, and the answer-by
   date for the topics that carry a legal clock.

   **It must NEVER quote the sender's own words back.** Anyone can type a
   message here and put somebody else's address in the email field, and this
   mail then carries attacker-chosen text to that person, from our domain, with
   our sending reputation behind it. That is a spam reflector, and building one
   by accident is exactly how a small project's mail domain gets blocklisted
   (owner 2026-08-27: "we can't send the receiver the message content to
   themselves to prevent spam abuse").

   So the body carries only values WE chose: the reference and the topic, from
   a fixed list. The reference alone is enough to chase a message, and the
   confirmation page prints it too.

   Inline styles only, like every mail here: clients ignore the CSP and mostly
   require inline styles anyway (docs/TODO.md, the style-src item). #}
{% extends 'emails/_base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'support.email.ack_subject'|trans({'%reference%': reference}, null, locale) }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">{{ 'support.email.ack_headline'|trans([], null, locale) }}</p>

  <p style="margin:0 0 14px">{{ 'support.email.ack_body'|trans([], null, locale) }}</p>

  <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin:0 0 18px">
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:4px 14px 4px 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a6a3f">{{ 'support.email.ack_reference_label'|trans([], null, locale) }}</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px">{{ reference }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding:4px 14px 4px 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a6a3f">{{ 'support.email.ack_topic_label'|trans([], null, locale) }}</td>
      <td style="padding:4px 0;font-size:14px">{{ topic_label }}</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  {# No answer-by date here. The deadline is OURS to meet, and it belongs on the
     desk notification, which is where somebody can act on it. Printing it to
     the sender turns an internal commitment into a promise on a specific day,
     and the first time we are a day late it reads as a broken one (owner
     2026-08-27). #}

  {# No echo of what they wrote. See the header of this file: it would make
     this mail a spam reflector. #}
  <p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#5a5d4d;line-height:1.55">
    {{ 'support.email.ack_no_reply'|trans([], null, locale) }}
  </p>
{% endblock %}
